    "body": "## Problem\r\nOn NetBSD, `man -w open` can return the exact manpage path, but `:Man` may still fail when man directories cannot be discovered from `manpath -q`, bare `man -w`, or `$MANPATH`.\r\nCloses #25919\r\n## Solution\r\nFall back to the direct manpage lookup when directory discovery fails. Add a regression test for resolving `open(2)` through `goto_tag()` without manpath data.",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-27T13:20:46Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40421#discussion_r3478195947"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/40421"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3478195947"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "each it() starts a new nvim instance, thus there is no need to restore \"mocks\".\n\nplease review https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#ai-assisted-work\n\n, then review this entire PR and leave a comment when it's updated",
            "commit_id": "28518557f42bb75ec736243e4ea2115c2fdffc23",
            "created_at": "2026-06-25T23:08:39Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -303,6 +303,39 @@ describe(':Man', function()\n     )\n   end)\n \n+  it('uses direct manpage lookup if man directories cannot be determined #25919', function()\n+    eq(\n+      {\n+        {\n+          name = 'open',\n+          filename = 'man://open(2)',\n+          cmd = '1',\n+        },\n+      },\n+      exec_lua(function()\n+        local man = require('man')\n+        local npcall = vim.npcall\n+        local find_path = man._find_path\n+\n+        vim.npcall = function()\n+          return nil\n+        end\n+        man._find_path = function(name, sect)\n+          if name == 'open' and sect == '2' then\n+            return '/usr/share/man/man2/open.2'\n+          end\n+        end\n+\n+        local ok, ret = pcall(man.goto_tag, 'open(2)')\n+        vim.npcall = npcall\n+        man._find_path = find_path",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40421#discussion_r3478195947",
            "id": 3478195947,
